<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baloch</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baluch, Baluchi people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baloch are an Iranian people living mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, a region divided between south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, with communities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and the Gulf. They speak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochi-language">Balochi</a>, are largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Muslims and were traditionally organised in tribes of herders and farmers. Medieval Arabic and Persian writers record them in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> before their main movement eastwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baloch.jpg" alt="Baloch" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mostafameraji · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baloch_people_(8).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
